  "details": "`claude-faf-mcp` MCP tools accept a caller-controlled `path` argument and resolve it (`~` expansion + `path.resolve()`) straight into a filesystem read/write **without confining it to a trusted project directory**. An absolute path or `../` traversal is resolved and used as-is, so the server process can be made to read \u2014 and, via the file tools, write \u2014 files outside the intended `.faf` project context. The only remaining limit is OS file permissions.",
  "id": "GHSA-rr55-jp92-8wp2",
